From 65c9ff86cc8bfa95da4fb3a0946c31b22b7dccb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 22:02:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/18] refactor(mailbox): serve SMTP with go-smtp instead of a
 hand-written server

The IMAP and DKIM/DMARC layers already used github.com/emersion/go-imap and
go-msgauth, but SMTP was 604 lines of hand-written protocol handling. That
file was where all three protocol defects fixed in the previous commit lived:
unbounded line buffering, incomplete dot-unstuffing and lossy CRLF trimming.
go-smtp implements all of it, so replace the parser with its Backend/Session
interfaces and keep only the Gitea-specific behaviour.

The server now delegates command parsing, STARTTLS, SASL, DATA transparency,
SIZE advertisement, and the line, message and recipient limits to the library,
which is configured from the same [mailbox] settings as before. Gitea keeps
the session backend: authentication against Gitea accounts, sender ownership
checks, recipient resolution, DKIM signing on submission, inbound SPF/DKIM/DMARC
policy, and delivery into the database.

AUTH LOGIN is implemented locally as a sasl.Server because go-sasl provides
only a client for that mechanism, and several desktop clients still use it.

netListen moves to server.go now that both listeners share it.

Tests replace the parser unit tests, which no longer have a subject, with
exchanges against a real go-smtp server on a loopback port: submission
refusing a return path before AUTH, PLAIN and LOGIN rejecting bad
credentials, and SIZE/AUTH advertisement following configuration.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
